# Worker secrets for local development.
#
# `wrangler dev` loads this file's real counterpart, workers/.dev.vars, and
# injects each key as a binding on `env`. Copy it before your first run:
#
#   cp workers/.dev.vars.example workers/.dev.vars
#
# Production values are NOT set here — they live in the GitHub `production`
# environment and are pushed by .github/workflows/cloudflare-deploy.yml.
# Values are dotenv-quoted; ENV and BUSINESS_TZ come from wrangler.jsonc instead.

# Bearer token for /api/admin/*. Unset locks those routes (503) rather than
# opening them, so a blank value here is safe but useless.
#   curl localhost:8787/api/admin/appointments -H "authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_TOKEN"
# Generate a real one for production with: openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_TOKEN="local-dev-token"

# Where new-booking notifications will go once notification is wired up.
# Unset disables notification entirely; leave these as-is for local work.
NOTIFY_EMAIL_TO="dev@example.com"
NOTIFY_EMAIL_FROM="bookings@example.com"

# Turnstile secret for the booking form's bot check. Unset (the default here)
# skips verification so you can book locally without the real secret; the
# widget still renders, since localhost is a registered domain on it.
# To exercise the check, use Cloudflare's always-passes / always-fails test
# secrets: 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA / 2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""
